          "items": [
            {
              "source_text_id": "text_24",
              "content": "The FCS-90A controllers coordinate fixed-wing flight control surfaces across three orthogonal axes. Roll (longitudinal axis) is governed by differential deflection of wing-tip ailerons. Pitch (transverse axis) is modulated by elevators on the horizontal stabilizer to control the angle of attack. Yaw (vertical axis) is managed by the vertical rudder. Auxiliary surfaces include flaps for lift enhancement during low-speed phases, and spoilers for lift destruction during landing touchdown operations.",
              "role": "正文",
              "reference_position_legacy": "右侧正文",
              "reference_typography_legacy": "黑色，常规字号，常规字重"
            }
          ],
          "formatted_content": "The FCS-90A controllers coordinate fixed-wing flight control surfaces across three orthogonal axes. Roll (longitudinal axis) is governed by differential deflection of wing-tip ailerons. Pitch (transverse axis) is modulated by elevators on the horizontal stabilizer to control the angle of attack. Yaw (vertical axis) is managed by the vertical rudder. Auxiliary surfaces include flaps for lift enhancement during low-speed phases, and spoilers for lift destruction during landing touchdown operations.",
